{% set local_problem %}
<p>Trinity's housing stock includes older homes near downtown and newer construction along the highway corridor. Both face the same fundamental problem: traditional sectional gutters aren't built for Morgan County's weather.</p>

<p>Sectional gutters have seams every 10 feet, and each seam is a potential failure point. Over time — especially in our humid climate with heavy rainfall — these seams separate, leak, and allow water to reach places it shouldn't go. Behind the gutters, fascia boards rot. Around the foundation, water pools and causes damage.</p>

<p>Morgan County's red clay soil makes these problems worse. Unlike sandy soil that absorbs water, clay forces runoff to pool and spread. When gutters overflow, that water doesn't disappear — it accumulates around your foundation.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters eliminate the seam problem entirely. Custom-fabricated on-site to fit your home exactly, they have no weak points to fail. For Trinity homes, seamless gutters provide the reliable protection our weather demands.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are exactly what they sound like: continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike traditional sectional gutters (made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together), seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil — custom-cut to the exact length of each run on your home.</p>

<p>Why does this matter? Because seams are where gutters fail. Every joint in a sectional gutter system is a potential leak point, a place for debris to catch, and a weak spot that can separate over time.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Trinity home, feed in aluminum coil, and fabricate your gutters right in your driveway. What comes out is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your roofline.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
